<newsitem itemid="65584" id="root" date="1996-09-19" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Camas half year pretax profit falls.</title>
<headline>Camas half year pretax profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		1.10		   vs 1.53</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.25		   vs 1.25</p>
<p> Pretax		     4.9		    vs 6.7</p>
<p> Turnover		   192.4		  vs 196.3</p>
<p> Operating result	 6.49		   vs 9.18</p>
<p> Exceptional		1.07 profit	  vs 0.13 profit</p>
<p> Interest		   2.66		   vs 2.60</p>
<p> Tax			  1.55		   vs 2.05</p>
<p> Net taxed		  3.36		   vs 4.66</p>
<p> Retained loss/profit   0.47 loss	    vs 0.84 profit</p>
<p> Pay date		   Dec 2</p>
<p> Div registration date  Oct 8</p>
<p> Ex-div date		Sept 30</p>
<p>Note - Camas Plc is a construction materials company.</p>
<p>Chief executive Alan Shearer said in a statement that the board expected &quot;a satisfactory performance in the second half of the year in the current market conditions,&quot; as the seasonally more favourable months are still to come.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
